<speak>I would rather arrange each meeting separately for now. A recurring entry has a way of staying in my calendar even after circumstances have changed. Then I see it on a busy morning and have to work out whether it is real or just an old placeholder. A clear description would help, though. If it is a telephone call, say telephone call; if it is a meeting at the branch, say that. I know it sounds obvious, but some invitations are so general that I cannot remember why I accepted them. At my age, I prefer the calendar to be helpful rather than mysterious.</speak>